    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Milwaukee Railroad laid tracks to the area in 1903, serving the logging industry and attracting outdoor enthusiasts who came to fish and hunt.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boulder_Junction%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Boulder Junction is home to Camp Manito-wish YMCA, which was founded in 1919.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boulder_Junction%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Much of the town is covered by the Northern Highland-American Legion State Forest, with headquarters on the east shore of Trout Lake.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
